  << /ActualText (\043 Global rules for codex\015\n\015\n\043\043 Operating principles\015\n\055 Prefer small\054 reviewable diffs\056 Avoid sweeping refactors unless explicitly requested\056\015\n\055 Before editing\054 identify the file\050s\051 to change and state the plan in 3\0556 bullets\056\015\n\055 Never invent APIs\054 configs\054 or file paths\056 If unsure\054 search the repo first\056\015\n\055 Keep changes consistent with existing style and architecture\056\015\n\015\n\043\043 Safety and secrets\015\n\055 Never paste secrets\054 tokens\054 private keys\054 \056env values\054 or credentials into code or logs\056\015\n\055 If a task requires secrets\054 ask me to provide them via environment variables\056\015\n\055 Do not add analytics\054 telemetry\054 or network calls unless I ask\056\015\n\015\n\043\043 Code quality bar\015\n\055 Add or update tests for behavior changes when the project has tests\056\015\n\055 Prefer type safety and explicit error handling\056\015\n\055 Add comments only when the intent is non\055obvious\056\015\n\015\n\043\043 Build and run etiquette\015\n\055 If you need to run commands\054 propose the exact command and why\056\015\n\055 When you make changes that may break build\054 run the fastest relevant check first\056\015\n\015\n\043\043 Output formatting\015\n\055 For code changes\072 include a short summary \053 list of files changed\056\015\n\055 For debugging\072 include hypotheses\054 experiments run\054 and the minimal fix\056\015\n\015\n\043\043 My preferences\015\n\055 I like concise explanations\054 concrete steps\054 and copy\055pastable commands\056\015\n\055 Default language for explanations\072 Chinese\056)
